{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-19T15:23:37.144Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"49b778ef43b03792a11c1946","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-19T15:23:37.144Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Implemented real-SDK pair scans and mutation guards. Focused pair regressions pass, including abstention, confidence authorization, explicit close gating, receipt history, read-only scans and model-unavailable refusal. Public evaluation inventory: 29 verified public copies; 2 skipped before tracker reads. Strict resolvable labels yield 35 positives (31 historical consolidation receipts plus 4 standard closures), paired with 70 lexical controls. Duplicate-group hashing separates dev and held-out items; retrieval misses count as false negatives. Calls run sequentially under nice."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-19T15:23:37.144Z"}],"before_hash":"36020894c84e6e2396836ba06197bbc3fd99d9c8b5157abfb61ec00c6ee8ed04","after_hash":"4541ded14f88bd048c884246990a9453b7ec51cb7cec69ef2c2b983eb239032a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7e0eefb5985604dcebd717daf3e610f7bb0d34858ed88e54fb17f4469488db7c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-19T15:27:55.026Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"49b778ef43b03792a11c1946","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-19T15:27:55.026Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Independent behavioral revert proofs: disabling only the positive probability cutoff makes the real-tracker apply regression fail (duplicate versus abstain); forcing closure without checking the extra close flag makes it fail (closed versus open). Source restored byte-for-byte; the same focused test passes 1/1. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pair apply writes only above threshold\" test/dedupe.test.ts. Threshold selection is dev-F1 with a 0.8 model floor; this is an operating-point calibration, not a 95% precision guarantee. Lexical controls are closed-world labels and may contain unrecorded duplicates."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-19T15:27:55.026Z"}],"before_hash":"4541ded14f88bd048c884246990a9453b7ec51cb7cec69ef2c2b983eb239032a","after_hash":"d4230ed354252a78ed5dd19352bf17cae005d53ff278491c5671a0fd13992450","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"96edb044ec765ddcde078ffd1991477da28a8ae93b511e8b7cb0d0fd57bb8e02"}
